  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U11U-READ-1",
      "title": "A Day on the Solar Farm",
      "text": "Last month our class visited a farm that runs on solar energy. The owner is a charming old man who can handle every machine by himself. He told us that the farm grows two crops a year, and the harvest in October is the biggest one. We helped him collect eggs, and the smell in the henhouse was a slight problem for some of us. After lunch, one student left a candle near a paper box, and a small fire started. The owner put out the fire in a second and asked us to blow out every candle before we left. Our classroom at school is often a mess, but on the farm we cleaned everything. To our delight, the owner gave each of us a bag of rice."
    }
  ],
